        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Look at 18 and 19. Latin counts them backward from twenty: *duodeviginti* means \"two taken from twenty\", *undeviginti* means \"one taken from twenty\". The pattern repeats in every ten: 28 is *duodetriginta*, 29 is *undetriginta*."
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Number",
