    {
      "title": "Three numbers that change, and ordinals",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Only *unus*, *duo* and *tres* change outfits like adjectives. The rest stay put, even when their noun changes."
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Job",
            "one (masc, fem, neut)",
            "two",
            "three"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "subject",
              "unus, una, unum",
              "duo, duae, duo",
              "tres, tres, tria"
            ],
            [
              "object",
              "unum, unam, unum",
              "duos, duas, duo",
              "tres, tres, tria"
            ],
            [
              "of",
              "unius",
              "duorum, duarum",
              "trium"
            ],
            [
              "with/in",
              "uno, una, uno",
              "duobus, duabus",
              "tribus"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "For example: *unus amicus* (one friend), *unam epistulam scribo* (I'm writing one letter), *cum duabus puellis* (with two girls), *tria templa* (three temples). From four on, nothing changes: *quattuor puellas video*, *cum quattuor amicis*."
        },
        {
          "type": "sub",
          "text": "Ordinal numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "tabel",
          "head": [
            "Order",
