        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Reading Roman numerals",
          "items": [
            "A smaller sign **after** a bigger one is added: VI = 6, XII = 12, LX = 60.",
            "A smaller sign **before** a bigger one is subtracted: IV = 4, IX = 9, XL = 40, XC = 90, CM = 900.",
            "The Romans themselves often wrote IIII, not IV — look at old clocks that still use it. The subtraction rule only became standard long after Roman times.",
            "Practice: MCMXLV = 1945; MMXXVI = 2026; XIX = 19; XLIV = 44."
          ]
        }
